First, let's find an expression for $H'(x)$ in terms of $f'$ and $g'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}H'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}H(x)&&\gray{\text{Equivalent notation}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)-3g(x)+5]&&\gray{\text{Substitute the expression for }H(x)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[2f(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}[3g(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}(5)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=2f'(x)-3g'(x)+0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $H'(x)=2f'(x)-3g'(x)$.
